      },
      "displayName": "Esmé Cowles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5fca89892730d8007611d907\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5fca89892730d8007611d907\" data-account-id=\"5fca89892730d8007611d907\" accountid=\"5fca89892730d8007611d907\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Benjamin Armintor</a>, I was going to open a separate ticket for using If-Match on PUT-to-update, but I remember now that the problem with that is that we only have weak ETags, because of the non-fixed nature of RDF not allowing for byte-for-byte certainty.  We've previously discussed If-Unmodified-Since as an alternative — would you be amenable to supporting that in Cavendish?</p>",
